       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg/day. The usual maximum for a single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **1600 mg/day total** in some other split\n- **Something else**, if you really want 1600 mg per dose. In that case, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order."
